o recurse into nested dict tables would break the existing pinned test tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:150, which asserts _emit_toml({'jira': {'nested': {'k': 'v'}}}) RAISES cfg.ConfigError for a nested sub-table; this test is an unenumerated consumer and the change reverses _emit_toml's current fail-closed contract on nested tables.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4b434be08c359853","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Serialization ('extend _config_writer._emit_toml to recurse into nested dict tables … today it stops at one level'); Scope ('Extend _config_writer.py _emit_toml for nested tables')","norm_id":"n0c377cb5d5ca5965","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI runs test_jira_onboard.py after the _emit_toml extension: the nested-sub-table case no longer raises, and the assertion fails."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the _emit_toml recursion extension with the existing fail-closed contract: name test_jira_onboard.py:150 (which asserts nested sub-tables RAISE), state whether that test is updated/replaced, and preserve fail-closed behavior for value types the recursive emitter still cannot model.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.25,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["_config_writer.py:84-87 deliberately raises ConfigError on a nested sub-table ('rebar's config writer supports only top-level keys and one level of [section]').","tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:149-150: `with pytest.raises(cfg.ConfigError): cfg._emit_toml({\"jira\": {\"nested\": {\"k\": \"v\"}}})  # nested sub-table` — an existing test pins the fail-closed behavior the plan wants to remove.","The docstring at _config_writer.py:43-51 frames fail-closed-on-nested as a corruption-safety guarantee, not an incidental limitation."],"finding":"The plan proposes extending _emit_toml to recurse into nested tables, but an existing regression test asserts the opposite contract (nested sub-tables must RAISE), and the plan never reconciles this.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe7578dc9b6e9338e","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Serialization (concrete): 'extend _config_writer._emit_toml to recurse into nested dict tables, emitting dotted headers … today it stops at one level.'","norm_id":"nff2aaec6c57817da","priority":0.85,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer extends _emit_toml for recursion; the existing test_jira_onboard.py test suite goes red.","Reviewer of the eventual PR is surprised a safety contract was silently loosened."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add to the Serialization section that test_jira_onboard.py's nested-sub-table `pytest.raises` case will be updated to reflect the new dotted-table support, while the datetime/unsupported-scalar fail-closed branch is retained unchanged.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py` (`test_emit_toml_fails_closed_on_unsupported_type`, lines 149-150) to the `_emit_toml` change inventory and specify how its nested-sub-table `ConfigError` assertion is reconciled with the new recursion behavior.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope: \"Extend `_config_writer.py` `_emit_toml` for nested tables (kept <cap).\"","Plan Serialization: \"extend `_config_writer._emit_toml` to recurse into nested dict tables, emitting dotted headers (`[mapping.projects.KEY.status_map]`); today it stops at one level.\"","Current guard `_config_writer.py:84-87` raises ConfigError for a nested sub-table.","Omitted patch site: `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py:149-150` `cfg._emit_toml({\"jira\": {\"nested\": {\"k\": \"v\"}}})` inside `pytest.raises(cfg.ConfigError)` — asserts the nested case raises."],"finding":"The plan proposes changing `_emit_toml` to recurse into nested dict tables, but its affected-file inventory for that change omits `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py`, which contains `test_emit_toml_fails_closed_on_unsupported_type` (lines 149-150) asserting that `_emit_toml({\"jira\": {\"nested\": {\"k\": \"v\"}}})` RAISES `ConfigError`. Making `_emit_toml` recurse into nested tables directly contradicts that existing assertion and breaks the test.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f458336c35cc5231c","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Serialization (concrete) / Scope: \"extend `_config_writer._emit_toml` to recurse into nested dict tables ... today it stops at one level\"","norm_id":"n9c9309e55313b373","priority":0.85,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py::test_emit_toml_fails_closed_on_unsupported_type — its second `pytest.raises(cfg.ConfigError)` on a nested sub-table starts failing once `_emit_toml` recurses instead of raising, an unpatched test the Scope does not name."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Update `test_emit_toml_fails_closed_on_unsupported_type` to keep a genuinely-unsupported type (e.g. datetime) as the fail-closed case and drop or invert the nested-sub-table assertion, since the new `_emit_toml` will emit nested tables as dotted headers rather than raise.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Guarantee fake-port fidelity to real pycontribs 3.x return shapes — capture at least one recorded real response per axis as the fake fixture source (or add a named, rationale'd child ticket for the live smoke), so the fake exercises the SAME parsing branches (esp. hierarchyLevel-present vs absent, createmeta required-field shape) the live path hits.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["E6","T2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A live smoke run is manual only, never a CI gate.'","E6(f): a proving command passing on a mock substitute that bypasses the new behavior does not prove the criterion","Parsing shapes (hierarchyLevel, createmeta required-field structure) are the risky new integration point — if the fake shape diverges from real, all four ACs stay green while the probe breaks live"],"finding":"All ACs are proven against a FAKE probe port with implementer-authored canned data; the plan defers the only real exercise of the new live code path to a 'manual smoke run, never a CI gate' with no named child or fidelity guarantee that the fake port's canned shapes match the real pycontribs 3.x return objects (e.g. IssueType.hierarchyLevel presence, createmeta_fieldtypes response structure).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb94fc1a5c3427372","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / Acceptance Criteria (all four); Approach 'default port built from build_client_from_settings ... tests inject a FAKE port'","norm_id":"n28a0eb6da38c4ada","priority":0.75,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["pycontribs 3.8 IssueType lacks hierarchyLevel and the fake wrongly supplies it — the hierarchy-drop branch is never exercised","createmeta_fieldtypes real shape differs from the fake, so create_defaults stubs are wrong live but tests pass"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Seed the fake port from real recorded pycontribs responses (VCR-style fixtures) and add an AC asserting the hierarchyLevel-absent branch is exercised.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Repoint the create_defaults baseline anchor to the actual field-building symbol (`outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields`, invoked via `backend.map_local_to_remote`) and confirm the enumerated baseline fields against that source.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.355,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the outbound create path adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote) already supplies summary, description, issuetype, priority, assignee, and conditionally status and parent'","search_files: map_local_to_remote defined at src/.../adapters/jira/backend.py:73 and jira_datacenter/backend.py:121; the field-building helper is outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields (backend.py:83)"],"finding":"The create_defaults baseline field set is anchored to an imprecise symbol/location: the plan cites `adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote)`, but `map_local_to_remote` is defined in backend.py (jira/backend.py:73, jira_datacenter/backend.py:121) and delegates to `outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f713fa5101f5420ed","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria → 'create_defaults' baseline (concrete) paragraph","norm_id":"n8fd9149a00c46878","priority":0.595,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer opens outbound_fields.py:140-158 looking for map_local_to_remote and finds a different function, mis-deriving the baseline set that gates which required fields get a stub."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the recursive _emit_toml emits each table's own scalar keys before any child sub-table header at every level (scalar-first, then nested dotted tables), preserving TOML round-trip validity for mixed scalar+subtable levels.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1812,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Current _emit_toml (_config_writer.py:71-88) already separates top scalars from tables at the TOP level only via the `top`/`tables` split; a recursive version must apply that same scalar-first-then-subtable ordering at EVERY level to stay TOML-valid.","In TOML, any key/value line after a `[a.b]` header belongs to `a.b`; a table that holds both scalar keys and nested dicts will mis-nest its scalars if a sub-table header is emitted before them.","The `--write` path re-parses the emitted file with tomllib on the next run (deep-merge), so a mis-ordered emit corrupts the round-trip."],"finding":"The dotted-header recursion does not address TOML key-ordering: a table's own scalar keys must be emitted BEFORE any child sub-table header, or scalars will re-parse into the wrong (child) table.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7c1806378d6b8251","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Serialization (concrete): 'recurse into nested dict tables, emitting dotted headers ([mapping.projects.KEY.status_map])'","norm_id":"n00a2654ea0c4f827","priority":0.4188,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A [mapping.projects.KEY] level that carries scalar fields (e.g. a note/marker) alongside sub-tables like status_map emits the header first, so the scalars land under the last-declared child table on re-read."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Fix the create_defaults baseline citation: name the symbol at outbound_fields.py:140 as _map_local_to_jira_fields (the map_local_to_remote method that delegates to it lives at adapters/jira/backend.py:73).","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3578,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["backend.py:73 'def map_local_to_remote(' delegates to outbound_fields._map_local_to_jira_fields","outbound_fields.py:140-146 builds the baseline dict (summary/description/issuetype/priority/assignee) inside _map_local_to_jira_fields, not a symbol named map_local_to_remote"],"finding":"The Approach attributes the create baseline to 'adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote)', but map_local_to_remote is a method on adapters/jira/backend.py:73; outbound_fields.py:140 defines _map_local_to_jira_fields (which backend.map_local_to_remote delegates to). The file/line/content are correct; the method-name attribution is not.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd9160cb7cd6038b3","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — 'create_defaults' baseline paragraph ('adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158 (map_local_to_remote)')","norm_id":"nece7cff676f1d0e0","priority":0.3422,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer greps outbound_fields.py for map_local_to_remote and finds nothing, wasting time reconciling the mismatch."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Reword to '_map_local_to_jira_fields (adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py:140-158), which adapters/jira/backend.py:73 map_local_to_remote delegates to'.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the error-handling/degraded-mode behavior for each live probe read (e.g. surface a clean per-axis error, emit the axis empty with a note, and define a non-zero exit vs partial-success contract) and the empty-sample case for transition gathering.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan lists 7 distinct jira.JIRA read calls but never addresses failure surfacing","'search_issues(jql) ... to fetch one sample issue per discovered issue type' — no handling stated when a type has zero issues","No mention of what the CLI emits/exits with on a failed external call"],"finding":"The probe issues multiple live external reads (issue_types, priorities, issue_link_types, statuses, createmeta_*, search_issues, transitions) but the plan states no error handling or degraded-mode behavior for when any of these calls fails (network/auth error, project KEY not found, or no sample issue found for a discovered issue type).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fec6f7f729a1faba2","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Axis grounding / transition hints","norm_id":"n58042a7f2cdde939","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator runs suggest-mapping against a project with no issues of a given type","Jira returns an auth/permission error mid-probe","A bad PROJECT key yields a 404 from createmeta"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add to Approach: each axis getter catches jira exceptions and emits the axis empty with a best-effort note (mirroring the hierarchy-drop pattern); no-sample issue types skip transition gathering silently; the command exits non-zero only if the core vocabulary probe fails.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify command behavior for an unknown/invalid project key, a Jira auth/transport error, and an empty-vocab / zero-sample-issue project (clear error vs. graceful empty emit).","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ACs cover emit, read-only, write-preserves-edits, transitions-best-effort but none covers an unknown project key, an auth/transport error, or an empty createmeta/vocab response","\"transition hints (best-effort) → ... fetch one sample issue per discovered issue type\" — behavior when search_issues returns zero samples is only implied, not stated"],"finding":"The command is user-facing but the plan names non-happy paths only for hierarchy-absent, global-status limitation, and partial transitions. It does not specify behavior for an invalid/unknown PROJECT key, a Jira auth/transport failure, or empty vocabulary / zero sample issues from search_issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4f8c9115cb655fe2","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Probe / Axis grounding; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"na621f36361ef3201","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["User runs `rebar bridge suggest-mapping BADKEY` and the probe raises a raw pycontribs exception instead of a clear error","A project with no issues yields no transition samples; unclear whether emit proceeds with empty hints or errors"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a line stating that an unknown project or auth failure surfaces a clear CLI error (non-zero exit, no partial write), and that empty vocab / zero transition samples emit an empty layer with a best-effort note rather than crashing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the `create_defaults`/createmeta axis with the deliberate 'createmeta pre-flight out of scope' decision at docs/user-guide.md:621-629: either justify why emitting *config stubs* (not written values) is distinct and safe, narrow the axis, or drop createmeta and update the doc.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.615,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'create_defaults stubs → jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>) + createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <issuetypeId>) (documented public createmeta API). A stub is emitted ONLY for a required: true field whose id/name is NOT already in the outbound create BASELINE'","docs/user-guide.md:621-629: 'A `createmeta` pre-flight is deliberately out of scope, and that is the mature answer rather than a gap. Jira's /rest/api/2/issue/createmeta can enumerate a project's required fields ... rebar does not ... A sync bridge cannot invent a meaningful value for an arbitrary required custom field; guessing one writes plausible-looking wrong data'","docs/user-guide.md:617: 'rebar does not discover or populate custom required fields'"],"finding":"The proposed `create_defaults`/createmeta-driven required-field discovery reintroduces functionality the codebase explicitly and deliberately rejected as out-of-scope, without acknowledging or reconciling with that prior decision.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f529edef1cd978157","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → create_defaults axis; Acceptance Criteria → create_defaults baseline paragraph","norm_id":"n6b3ef7969eff1923","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or maintainer sees the new suggest-mapping command emitting createmeta-derived required-field stubs and concludes rebar now supports custom-required-field discovery, contradicting the documented boundary.","The emitted create_defaults stubs invite operators to fill in guessed values for arbitrary required custom fields — exactly the 'plausible-looking wrong data' the doc warns against."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a criterion (or note) confirming the _emit_toml nested-table extension leaves existing single-level callers (write_jira_config) output unchanged — a regression test on the existing emit path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T4","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'extend _config_writer._emit_toml to recurse into nested dict tables'","write_jira_config is an existing consumer of _emit_toml","No AC covers regression of the existing single-level emit behavior"],"finding":"The plan extends the existing `_config_writer._emit_toml` to recurse into nested tables, changing a function today documented to 'stop at one level', but names no verification that existing single-level callers (e.g. write_jira_config) produce byte-identical output after the change.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ffe8225d76b86fc24","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Serialization (concrete) — 'extend _config_writer._emit_toml ... today it stops at one level'","norm_id":"n2f7dc184dbd92c69","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future write_jira_config call now emits nested tables it previously flattened or errored on"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add AC: 'test_emit_toml_single_level_unchanged — existing write_jira_config output is byte-identical after the nested-table extension.'","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a test feeding the fake port an empty/error response (empty vocab, zero sample issues, unknown-project signal) and assert the command degrades gracefully rather than crashing.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Four ACs all assert happy-path emit/read-only/merge/transitions-partial; none feeds the fake port an error or empty response","\"Automated tests use a FAKE probe port returning canned ... data\" — canned data is well-formed in every listed AC"],"finding":"The AC suite exercises the probe only through a FAKE port; there is no acceptance criterion covering error/empty responses from that port (unknown project, empty createmeta, zero search_issues results), so the emit/merge logic's non-happy paths go untested.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f32c77026b527a7c0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing / Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n595d9e32096e8a81","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A regression that crashes on empty createmeta or a missing project would still pass the four green ACs"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Add `test_probe_handles_empty_and_error` covering an empty createmeta / zero search_issues fake and an unknown-project signal, asserting a clear error or empty-layer emit with note.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the createmeta_fieldtypes capability assertion: confirm it exists (or pin to project_issue_fields as the non-deprecated replacement) across the entire jira>=3.8,<4 range, and note the deprecation in the plan.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["jira.readthedocs.io 3.10.6.dev docs (within the <4 pin) emit: \"'createmeta_fieldtypes' is deprecated and will be removed in future releases. Use 'project_issue_fields' instead.\"","pycontribs/jira issue #1802 'Breaking changes between v3.5.2 and v3.6.0': createmeta_fieldtypes renamed to project_issue_fields; the release removed/renamed methods WITHOUT bumping the major version, so a <4 pin does not guarantee the method name is stable","sg-jira-bridge (prior art) uses createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes for exactly this Server-9 createmeta case, confirming the API family is real but also confirming the naming churn","grep of src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters for 'createmeta' returns no matches — this method is net-new to the repo, so the deprecation risk is not covered by any existing in-repo usage"],"finding":"The plan asserts createmeta_fieldtypes / createmeta_issuetypes as 'documented public createmeta API' on the pinned jira>=3.8,<4 client, but retrieved sources indicate createmeta_fieldtypes is DEPRECATED within that pin range in favor of project_issue_fields, so the capability assertion is only partly resolved.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff9a2a1a13f514cac","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Axis grounding, 'create_defaults stubs → jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>) + createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <issuetypeId>) (documented public createmeta API)'","norm_id":"n008ec1e8c150bfa1","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Operator on a jira-python build near the <4 ceiling where createmeta_fieldtypes was removed/renamed: the create_defaults probe raises AttributeError at runtime","A DeprecationWarning surfaces in the emitted output or CI, undermining the 'documented public' framing"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"State that create_defaults is grounded in createmeta_issuetypes + project_issue_fields (the non-deprecated 3.x method), with createmeta_fieldtypes only as a documented fallback for older 3.8–3.5 clients, and have the probe degrade the create_defaults axis (emit empty + best-effort note, like the hierarchy axis) when neither method is present.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Verify each named getter (issue_types, priorities, issue_link_types, statuses, createmeta_issuetypes, createmeta_fieldtypes) exists with the assumed signature on the pinned jira>=3.8,<4 client against pycontribs docs/--help, and cite the confirming source (or route to a short SPIKE) rather than asserting 'documented public'.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'every axis uses a HIGH-LEVEL method (no private REST)' listing issue_types(), priorities(), issue_link_types(), statuses(), createmeta_issuetypes/fieldtypes","search_files across the repo found NO in-repo use of any of these getters (contrast search_issues and transitions, which ARE confirmed in-repo)","resolve_symbol for jira.JIRA.issue_types / createmeta_issuetypes / createmeta_fieldtypes all returned UNRESOLVED — jira is an optional extra not installed, so the specific method surface is Unverified (Partially-verified: client used in-repo, these methods unconfirmed)"],"finding":"The vocabulary/createmeta getters the probe grounds each axis in (issue_types(), priorities(), issue_link_types(), statuses(), createmeta_issuetypes(), createmeta_fieldtypes()) are asserted as 'documented public pycontribs 3.x API' but are NEW surfaces used nowhere in-repo and were not verified against the pinned jira>=3.8,<4 client's actual method set (the jira lib is an uninstalled optional extra).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8d048b30ce71c8c4","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Axis grounding' bullets; pyproject.toml:202 (jira>=3.8,<4)","norm_id":"n53d72243439261de","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A method name or signature differs on the pinned 3.8–3.x client (e.g. renamed/removed getter) and the probe fails at runtime after ship, defeating the 'read-only, offline-testable' value since the fake port would encode a signature the real client does not honor"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes are supported against Jira Data Center 8.14+ (not just Cloud) on the pinned client, or state the DC createmeta surface used and its verification source.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'create_defaults stubs → jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes(<KEY>) + createmeta_fieldtypes(<KEY>, <issuetypeId>) (documented public createmeta API)'","transport docstring: 'Auth is Bearer PAT ... Jira 8.14+' — a Data Center deployment","docs/user-guide.md:621-629 explicitly scopes a createmeta pre-flight OUT for this integration, so no existing DC createmeta usage exists to anchor these method names/behavior"],"finding":"createmeta_issuetypes/createmeta_fieldtypes are the pycontribs 3.x SPLIT-createmeta helpers oriented to Jira Cloud's per-issuetype createmeta endpoints, but this transport targets Jira Data Center; the plan does not confirm these split methods are available/behave correctly against DC 8.14+.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5d6fa2beb1df39d0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → create_defaults bullet; transport.py:156 ('the real jira.JIRA client' for DC, Bearer PAT / Jira 8.14+)","norm_id":"n40166e30cb8b0165","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The split-createmeta methods target endpoints present on Cloud but shaped differently (or the older monolithic createmeta) on the DC server the transport connects to, so create_defaults discovery returns unexpected shapes or errors against a real DC instance"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how `--write` handles the read-mutate-replace window (accept last-writer-wins as documented CLI scope, or note single-user assumption) so the 'hand edits never clobbered' claim is bounded to keys present at read time.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8263,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Read with tomllib, DEEP-MERGE under [mapping.projects.<KEY>] with EXISTING keys winning (hand edits never clobbered), re-emit whole, atomic os.replace.\"","atomic os.replace makes the final write atomic but does not close the read->replace window; 'existing keys win' only protects keys present at READ time, not edits made during the window"],"finding":"The `--write` mode reads the whole config file, deep-merges, and atomically replaces it, but there is no guard against a read-mutate-write TOCTOU: a concurrent second `suggest-mapping --write` (or a hand-edit landing between the tomllib read and the os.replace) is silently clobbered because the in-memory merged copy overwrites whatever the file became.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"feedca2fceadbd3fb","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — `--write`: mirror write_jira_config's read-whole/mutate/re-emit/atomic-replace pattern","norm_id":"n2d8c8694c59616cf","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two `suggest-mapping --write` runs (or a run overlapping a manual edit) race: the later os.replace wins wholesale, dropping the interleaved edit despite the 'existing keys win' promise"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Document that `--write` is a single-user, last-writer-wins operation whose 'existing keys win' guarantee covers only keys present when the file was read; note it is not concurrency-safe against edits made during the probe.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the _config_writer.py path from src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_config_writer.py to src/rebar/_config_writer.py (re-exported via rebar.config) in the Approach, Scope, and Serialization sections.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["search_files found _emit_toml/write_jira_config only in src/rebar/_config_writer.py and re-exported at src/rebar/config.py:97-98","search of src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler for _emit_toml and write_jira_config returned (no matches)","_config_writer.py:1 docstring: 'The config WRITE path — rebar's only writer of a reba